15 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a machine learning pipeline for predicting plant stress class from an input leaf image using processes including EfficientNet feature extraction, patch tokenization, projection embedding, LSTM-based sequence modeling, entanglement attention fusion, global max pooling, dense layers, and sigmoid activation, resulting in a predicted class label. Color coding denotes input, feature extraction, tokenization and embedding, sequence modeling, fusion and pooling, and prediction.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Flowchart outlining the OLID-I plant stress classification pipeline, detailing dataset structure, preprocessing, model embedding, tri-directional LSTM feature learning, attention fusion, classification, training, evaluation, and final prediction of plant stress class.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Bar chart titled \215Q-TriLSTM-Vision Improvement Margin vs ViT-B/16\216 compares F1 score improvements for two categories. Left panel shows per-crop improvements, with BitterGourd having the highest delta F1 of 0.034 and Cucumber the lowest at 0.022. Right panel shows per-stress-type improvements, with Disease having the highest delta F1 of 0.033 and Healthy the lowest at 0.018. All improvements are positive, indicating Q-TriLSTM outperforms ViT-B/16 for both crop and stress categories.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Grid of eight confusion matrices compares classification results for plant health scenarios\204Healthy, Disease, Insect, Nutrient Deficiency\204across models Q-TriLSTM-Vision, DenseNet-121, ViT-B/16, BiLSTM-CNN, EfficientNet-B0, Plain-LSTM, ResNet-50, and VGG-16, displaying performance differences through predicted and actual class probabilities.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Bar chart and horizontal bar graph comparing model architecture and component ablations on Macro-F1 scores. Top chart shows changes in Macro-F1 relative to the full Q-TriLSTM-Vision model, with the largest drops from removing vision encoder, TriLSTM, and ResNet-50 backbone. Bottom chart presents absolute Macro-F1 scores for each configuration, highlighting 0.9127 for the full model and reduced scores for ablations, with dashed line marking the full model's performance.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Line graph comparing Macro-F1 scores versus decision thresholds for four categories: Healthy \(green\), Nutritional Deficiency \(blue\), Disease \(red\), and Insect \(orange\). Healthy achieves the highest maximum score, peaking near decision threshold 0.5, indicated by the largest green point. Other categories have slightly lower peaks, each marked by colored points near their optimal threshold. A dashed vertical line marks the fixed threshold at 0.5 across all curves. Labels are clearly annotated within the plot area.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
